WEBVTT

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.720
Speaker 1: All right, so I want to answer a question about assurance of salvation.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:28.160
Speaker 1: This is something that is, I. I think very simple, but a lot of people still don't get it, especially in the body of Christ.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:40.290
Speaker 1: And we want to know first and foremost what the Bible teaches about it and how believers should think about this.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:53.410
Speaker 1: So first and foremost, you have to realize that even from the Old Testament, the Bible is very definite about what people should think about assurance of salvation.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:01:06.000
Speaker 1: When you look at the text, like Isaiah, chapter 32, verse 17, Isaiah 32, 17, he says, the work of righteousness will be peace, and the effect of righteousness will be quietness and assurance forever.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.800
Speaker 1: You see, the Bible tells us what righteousness will produce in the believer.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.960
Speaker 1: The work of righteousness will be peace, it says, and the effect of righteousness will be what?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.400
Speaker 1: Quietness and assurance forever.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:30.570
Speaker 1: God doesn't want you petrified, constantly doubting if you have received what you've received.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:36.130
Speaker 1: God does not pander to the antics of man, the politics of man.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:54.930
Speaker 1: You know, when man is giving you something, sometimes he wants to rub it in, you know, maybe just as an ungodly way to make you grateful, just sometimes make you feel unsure about the agreement that you have.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.490
Speaker 1: Well, God doesn't need to do that.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.490
Speaker 1: The Bible is very definite about what the product of righteousness will be.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.130
Speaker 1: Peace and quietness forever.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:13.450
Speaker 1: This should give you a lot of excitement and should stir up a lot of praise in your heart to the Lord.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:14.890
Speaker 1: Hallelujah.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:23.160
Speaker 1: So it means as a believer, you ought to know that you know that you have assurance.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:31.360
Speaker 1: And yeah, I can assure you, once in a while, even the most sanctified might have doubts.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.720
Speaker 1: But you see, those doubts stem from ignorance.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.520
Speaker 1: Those doubts stem from ignorance, all right.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:49.840
Speaker 1: Because, you see, growing up in a culture, growing up in a world where everything is earned.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.040
Speaker 1: That's the culture.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.560
Speaker 1: That's how we are wired, and that's how we are conditioned.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:09.680
Speaker 1: So when it now comes to God, and he says, believe, demonstrate fruits, but not as a Pericles, but as a result of your faith.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:21.490
Speaker 1: When we have periods where we think our devotion hasn't been as consistent, we wonder, does God still love us?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.850
Speaker 1: Do I still have assurance?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:32.050
Speaker 1: Because we think of the human relationships that we've had and what a man will do in those situations.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:41.400
Speaker 1: If man was God, like if it was our boss and we had a period where we're not coming to work, the next thing a threat is going to follow.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.720
Speaker 1: But he says, the effect of righteousness shall be quietness and peace forever.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.760
Speaker 1: One of my favorite go to texts for assurance is Philippians 1:6.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:59.000
Speaker 1: And this is because it is one thing for you to have personal assurance.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:08.990
Speaker 1: After all, everybody says salvation is personal, but to have assurance about others, that's a totally different new level.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:09.950
Speaker 1: And this is what I mean.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:18.230
Speaker 1: Paul says, and being confident of this very thing, that he who has begun a good work in you will complete it until the day of Jesus Christ.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.990
Speaker 1: So a pastor is looking at his congregation and saying this.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:29.070
Speaker 1: I am confident he who has begun a good work in you will perform it.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:32.950
Speaker 1: So, number one, it means he has assurance of their salvation.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:43.150
Speaker 1: Listen, it is true that faith is stared from the deeper recesses of a man's heart, a place where a normal human eye cannot witness.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:56.430
Speaker 1: And so in that sense, it is only in your heart that you know that you truly believed and that faith was mixed, you know, and had contact with the Holy Spirit that made salvation efficacious in your spirit.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:57.550
Speaker 1: So it's.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.400
Speaker 1: It's inward.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.200
Speaker 1: All right?

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:09.160
Speaker 1: So it is just the profession of your faith, your corresponding action, that can help us know that you are saved by the fruits.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.200
Speaker 1: You shall know them.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.720
Speaker 1: Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:21.320
Speaker 1: But I'm saying that when Paul saw the profession of their faith corresponding action, it was sufficient for him.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.600
Speaker 1: All right, some.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.540
Speaker 1: Some people think you are a good pastor when you always tell people you may end up in hell.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.740
Speaker 1: Now, some people preach like that to shake people up.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:43.340
Speaker 1: So it is quite instructive that Paul will say, I am confident of this one thing.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.980
Speaker 1: He who has begun a good work in you will perform it.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.380
Speaker 1: Oh, my God, what a pastor.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:06:08.470
Speaker 1: There are some pastors who think it's a teaching on holiness to scare people and tell them they just might not make it after 30 years of service in church, to scare people and tell them it doesn't matter your title, you know, and all of that.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:14.030
Speaker 1: But when Paul says, being confident of this very thing, he who has begun a good work in you.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:32.480
Speaker 1: You see, when you preach like that, even the people who have inconsistencies, you have stirred up the efficacy of the Holy Spirit in them, staring them to drop any of such foolish inconsistencies.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.240
Speaker 1: This is how to preach.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.000
Speaker 1: When Paul says, what?

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.720
Speaker 1: Know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost?

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:44.170
Speaker 1: What do you not know what a way to preach?

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.410
Speaker 1: I want to preach like Paul, okay?

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:57.490
Speaker 1: And then he says, he who has begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:01.410
Speaker 1: You see, many times we struggle with the concept of assurance.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:04.170
Speaker 1: Because we don't trust ourselves, and rightly so.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.370
Speaker 1: If we trust ourselves, we'll be in trouble.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:19.140
Speaker 1: But when you base your conviction of assurance on God, it changes the ball game.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:36.430
Speaker 1: Being confident of this very thing, that he who has begun a good work will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ, meaning the Holy Spirit is going to preserve, guide and guard what he has started in your life.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.270
Speaker 1: You know, has it ever happened?

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:43.870
Speaker 1: You had a candle in a windy place and you had to protect that fire.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.790
Speaker 1: The Holy Spirit preserves you.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:51.710
Speaker 1: And when it comes to trusting him, oh my God, then you can rest assured.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.710
Speaker 1: Assurance is indeed a thing.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:59.950
Speaker 1: Being confident of this very thing, he who has begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:07.570
Speaker 1: And my next favorite one, especially Jude verse, you know, the Book of Jude.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:23.730
Speaker 1: After he had talked about a lot of people who crept in unawares, you know, and were pretending to be part of the believing folk flock, but were not.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.140
Speaker 1: Now he talks to the believers.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:37.500
Speaker 1: He says, now to him that is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you faultless before the presence of his glory, with exceeding joy.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.220
Speaker 1: Listen, there are some verses.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:09:00.790
Speaker 1: When I see them, I remember where I was at least the station in my life when I first encountered them and the effect they had in my life as a young believer who had many things to outgrow, many things to shed off.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.190
Speaker 1: When I saw this verse, it changed my life.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.310
Speaker 1: Jude verse 24.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:14.390
Speaker 1: Now, to him that is able to keep me from stumbling, he's able to keep me.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:19.030
Speaker 1: If it was my power, I'll be afraid, but he's able to keep me.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.350
Speaker 1: You know, I remember those days.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.430
Speaker 1: I'll pace the floor and thank him.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.190
Speaker 1: You're able to keep me from stumbling.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.430
Speaker 1: You're able to keep me from stumbling.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.950
Speaker 1: You're able to keep me.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:37.910
Speaker 1: You know, I was praying years ago and the Lord said, everything I need to teach and everything you need to learn, I'll teach you.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:49.120
Speaker 1: When God tells you that, you know that ignorance is not going to end your ministry, ignorance is not going to end your life.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:56.400
Speaker 1: He's able to keep me from stumbling and to present me faultless before the brains of his glory with exceeding joy.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.640
Speaker 1: All right?

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.360
Speaker 1: So at the end of the day you will know that the grace of God brought you thus far.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.720
Speaker 1: That, my brothers and sisters, is assurance.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.250
Speaker 1: At least you know, for beginning, for beginners.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:14.730
Speaker 1: And I believe that this has blessed you and stead you.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.530
Speaker 1: So that's what the Bible says.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:22.250
Speaker 1: All right, I want you to take some moments.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.930
Speaker 1: Don't just respond to this in theological, intellectual sense.

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:40.010
Speaker 1: But I want you to take some moments today to thank God to Him who is able to keep me from stumbling and to present me before the presence of his glory with exceeding joy.
